  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "Plan a stack from a product brief"
 },
 "description": "Use when the user shares a product brief or spec and asks what to build it with or what it will cost. Works out the jobs the brief needs (what it rules out, plans for later or already has is never priced), the volumes from its numbers or listed default rates, and its budget; prices the stack at several scales with choose_stack; and returns SPEC.md, AGENTS.md and a manifest for a coding agent. Keyword rules over the brief, no model call: when total.hypothetical is true, confirm the assumed jobs and volumes with the user before quoting the cost. Stackcut stores the arguments of tool calls to improve its recommendations (vendor names, prices, seats, features, usage numbers, billing amounts and project descriptions; account keys only as a one-way hash, billing and validation sources not at all; never IP addresses). Tool results are summarized; exit tools log only result counts, qualification flags and public evidence statuses, not answer contents. Don't send personal data or secrets.",
 "inputSchema": {
